Classification proof sketch for odd C:
  P(C)/C is multiplicative with local factor 1+a*(1-1/p) at p^a.
  A(C)=C iff P(C)/C=3.
  If 3 does not divide C, the two smallest odd-prime factors already
  give (9/5)*(13/7)>3, and one prime power never solves the equation.
  If 3^a || C: a=1 forces the remaining factor to be 9/5, hence 5;
  a=2 leaves a ratio below every odd-prime factor; a=3 gives 27;
  a>3 overshoots.  So the odd fixed clocks are exactly 15 and 27.

