  Which retained LRC carrier best preserves the floor/tight predicate.
Switch/gauges:
  proof transfer from aliquot fixed points, LRC proof utility,
  AP single-swap discrimination, and cost/availability.
Challenged assumption:
  Vertices need not be runners.  Considered runners, residues,
  antipodal shells, gcd strata, pair pinches, boundary events,
  carry fibers, and proof obligations.  This scout uses carrier
  lenses as vertices; the quotient preserves tight/floor evidence
  and destroys raw speed order.
