========================================================================
Research takeaways
========================================================================
1. The LRC n=14 clock C=27 is not just composite: it is one of
   exactly two odd Pillai-fixed clocks C with A(C)=C, the other
   being C=15 (n=8).
2. AP is shell-fixed.  Vstar is not shell-fixed, but it is fixed by
   the coarser gcd/divisor carrier: the missing shell 12 and doubled
   shell 3 both live in the gcd-3 stratum of C=27.
3. In the AP single-swap scan through n=14, every tight non-AP row
   preserves weighted gcd-shell mass.  This is a new necessary
   finite certificate target inspired directly by aliquot fixed points.
4. The open proof use is a no-leak lemma: once the carrier is fixed,
   pair-pinch/carry labels should force AP or the known Vstar floor
   row; every mass-changing row should be strictly loose.
